& \text { distance }(P, C D)=\sqrt{14^{2}-\left(\frac{28-14}{2}\right)^{2}}=7 \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

so the altitude of trapezoid $A B C D$ is $15 \sqrt{3}$, so the final answer is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot(14+18) \cdot 15 \sqrt{3}=345 \sqrt{3}$.

